IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, SECTIONS 5 AND 6: ENFORCEMENT BY THE PROMISEE; PROTECTION OF THE PROMISOR FROM DOUBLE LIABILITY.
--
-- What is encoded: s 5 (section 2 does not affect the promisee's right to enforce) and s 6 (the court or arbitral
-- tribunal must reduce an award to the third party where the promisee has recovered a sum).  The reduction itself
-- is "such extent as it thinks appropriate": a judgment handed to the court or tribunal, taken as an input and
-- never guessed.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not
-- answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").

§ `Section 5 -- enforcement of contract by promisee`

-- src:234 | 5. Section 2 does not affect any right of the promisee to enforce any
-- src:235 | term of the contract.
@ref s 5 (src:234-235)
GIVEN `the right asked about is a right of the promisee to enforce a term of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5 section 2 affects a right of the promisee to enforce a term of the contract` MEANS
    IF `the right asked about is a right of the promisee to enforce a term of the contract`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 2 does not affect any right of the promisee to enforce any term of the contract."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the negative reaches only "any right of the promisee to enforce any term of the contract"; another right is outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 6 -- protection of promisor from double liability`

-- src:243 | (a) the third party’s loss in respect of the term; or
@ref s 6(a) (src:243-243)
GIVEN `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` MEANS
    `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term`

-- src:245 | (b) the expense to the promisee of making good to the third
-- src:246 | party the default of the promisor,
@ref s 6(b) (src:245-246)
GIVEN `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(b) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` MEANS
    `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor`

-- The duty "arises" when the "Where" is met.  JUST FALSE: the where fails; NOTHING: the proceedings are not ones the
-- duty speaks of.
-- src:239 | 6. Where under section 2, a term of a contract is enforceable by a
-- src:240 | third party, and the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum
-- src:241 | in respect of —
-- src:243 | (a) the third party’s loss in respect of the term; or
-- src:245 | (b) the expense to the promisee of making good to the third
-- src:246 | party the default of the promisor,
-- src:248 | then, in any proceedings brought in reliance on that section by the
-- src:249 | third party, the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the
-- src:250 | third party to such extent as it thinks appropriate to take account of the
-- src:251 | sum recovered by the promisee.
@ref s 6 (src:239-251)
GIVEN `under section 2 a term of the contract is enforceable by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings are brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "any proceedings brought in reliance on that section by the third party"; other proceedings are outside it
        IF NOT `proceedings are brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "Where under section 2, a term of a contract is enforceable by a third party, and the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of — (a) ...; or (b) ..."
        IF NOT `under section 2 a term of the contract is enforceable by the third party` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; same ruling): "and the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of — (a) ...; or (b) ..."
        IF NOT (`s 6(a) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term`
                OR `s 6(b) the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The award after the reduction.  A number cannot carry JUST FALSE, so when the duty does not arise the answer is
-- NOTHING and the yes/no function above carries the no (assumed, not ruled: the twin of the ruling of 2026-11-05).
-- src:248 | then, in any proceedings brought in reliance on that section by the
-- src:249 | third party, the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the
-- src:250 | third party to such extent as it thinks appropriate to take account of the
-- src:251 | sum recovered by the promisee.
@ref s 6 the reduced award (src:248-251)
GIVEN `under section 2 a term of the contract is enforceable by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings are brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the award before the reduction` IS A NUMBER
      `the extent of the reduction the court or arbitral tribunal thinks appropriate` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 6 the award to the third party after the reduction` MEANS
    IF `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` `under section 2 a term of the contract is enforceable by the third party` `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` `proceedings are brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN CONSIDER `the extent of the reduction the court or arbitral tribunal thinks appropriate`
         -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "to such extent as it thinks appropriate" is a judgment handed to the court or tribunal, and the person has not stated it
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST reduction THEN
             IF reduction AT LEAST 0 AND reduction AT MOST `the award before the reduction`
             THEN JUST (`the award before the reduction` MINUS reduction)
             -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): a "reduction" below nothing, or by more than the award, is not one the text describes
             ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise, so no reduced award is stated; the yes/no function above carries the "no"
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `The regulative rule derived from s 6 (no time limit is stated, so none is given)`

-- The text names the bearer: "the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award".
-- src:248 | then, in any proceedings brought in reliance on that section by the
-- src:249 | third party, the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the
-- src:250 | third party to such extent as it thinks appropriate to take account of the
-- src:251 | sum recovered by the promisee.
@ref s 6 the duty (src:248-251)
GIVEN `under section 2 a term of the contract is enforceable by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings are brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal MUST reduce any award to the third party` MEANS
    IF `s 6 the court or arbitral tribunal must reduce any award to the third party` `under section 2 a term of the contract is enforceable by the third party` `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the third party's loss in respect of the term` `the promisee has recovered from the promisor a sum in respect of the expense to the promisee of making good to the third party the default of the promisor` `proceedings are brought in reliance on section 2 by the third party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court or arbitral tribunal` MUST `reduce the award to the third party`
    ELSE FULFILLED
